Let the app's own page write the clipboard in the Linux web view.

WebKit rejects navigator.clipboard.writeText and execCommand("copy") with
NotAllowedError unless the document has transient user activation. A click
delivered to the view inside JUCE's XEmbed window never grants it: the handler
runs with navigator.userActivation.isActive false, on a secure context with
focus, so every Copy button in the UI reported "Copy failed". A stock
WebKitGTK window on the same juce:// scheme copies fine from a click.

webkit_settings_set_javascript_can_access_clipboard is WebKit's own bypass of
that check (JUCE already binds the symbol but never calls it). It is set only
when native integrations are enabled, i.e. for a page the app serves itself; a
browser showing a third-party site keeps JUCE's default, which also keeps that
site from reading the clipboard.

--- a/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_linux.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_linux.cpp
@@ -932,6 +932,19 @@
         wk.juce_webkit_settings_set_enable_developer_extras (settings, true);
        #endif
 
+        // PLECTRIFY_WEBKIT_CLIPBOARD: let the app's own page write the
+        // clipboard. WebKit rejects navigator.clipboard.writeText (and
+        // execCommand("copy")) with NotAllowedError unless the document has
+        // transient user activation, and a click delivered to this view inside
+        // JUCE's XEmbed window never grants it: navigator.userActivation stays
+        // inactive in the click handler itself. So every Copy button failed.
+        // This setting is WebKit's own bypass of that check. Only for a view
+        // with native integrations, i.e. a page the app serves itself: a
+        // browser showing a third-party site keeps JUCE's default, which also
+        // keeps that site from reading the clipboard.
+        if (initialisationData->nativeIntegrationsEnabled)
+            wk.juce_webkit_settings_set_javascript_can_access_clipboard (settings, true);
+
         auto* webviewWidget = WebKitSymbols::getInstance()->juce_webkit_web_view_new_with_settings (settings);
         webview = (WebKitWebView*) webviewWidget;
 
